{"id":"machine_lateral_raise","name":"Machine lateral raise","cue":"Lead with your elbows; stop at shoulder height.","research":"Seated lateral raise machine (Hammer Strength / Life Fitness / Precor style: seat height set so the shoulder joints sit on the lever axes, upright back pad, a lever pad on the outer forearm near the elbow on each side). Both arms raise together in the frontal plane of the trunk: shoulder elevation 15 -> 90 deg (plane 0, rot 0), elbows fixed at 90 so the forearms stay level pointing forward and the pads ride on the outer forearms (underneath at the stretch, on top at the peak, pushing down). Trunk 10 deg behind vertical (back pad as the shoulder press), hips 82, knees 90, feet flat. Each lever hinges about the shoulder joint axis (the thorax anterior axis, tilted 10 deg with the trunk), so the pad never slides on the arm (skin gap 0.004 H at every phase); its hub and a cam sit behind the back pad, the rod runs behind the arm so nothing crosses the deltoid, and a cable over one pulley loads both cams from a stack behind the seat. Hands are left free (closed fists), the pads carry the load.","targets":{"tol":10,"A":{"trunk_flexion":-10,"hip_flexion":82,"knee_flexion":90,"shoulder_elevation":15,"shoulder_plane":0,"elbow_flexion":90},"B":{"shoulder_elevation":90,"shoulder_plane":0,"elbow_flexion":90}},"muscles":{"primary":["delt_lat"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":15,"el":5,"dAz":20,"dEl":20,"fill":0.64,"note":"Same view as the cable lateral raise (research az 15 / el 5, turned 20 deg and raised 20 deg: az 35 / el 25, 28 deg off the research view): the side delts face out at the stretch and up at the peak. The levers, hubs and stack sit behind the back pad, so nothing crosses the shoulders from this side."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"tempo":[1,0.5,2.5,0.5],"root":[0,0.298,0],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":-8},"lumbar":{"flex":-1},"thorax":{"flex":-1},"neck":{"flex":-4},"head":{"flex":-2},"thigh_l":{"flex":82,"abd":7},"shank_l":{"flex":9